# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The rule of thumb: **exclude only what is 100 % certain the build never
# reads, and that either churns a lot or is per-machine state.**  Everything
# else stays in.
#
# The build (build/docker/dist.dockerfile) needs exactly this much:
#
#   Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock      workspace manifest + lockfile
#   crates/                     all workspace crates (+ crates/admin/templates,
#                               which tailwind.config.js scans)
#   tests/                      workspace member "tests"
#   assets/                     tailwindcss.css + app.js (rust-embed snapshot)
#   tailwind.config.js          tailwind CLI config (content globs)
#   build/docker/               cargo-config.toml
#
# Source-level files are NEVER excluded — not even ones that look like
# junk.  A template that askama embeds, a YAML that include_str! reads, a
# SQL migration that include_str! embeds, a fixture a test include_bytes!'s:
# if it is missing the build breaks, or worse, produces a subtly wrong
# binary.  A few KB of context is a cheap insurance premium against a
# silent break.
#
# ⚠️  Docker's .dockerignore is NOT gitignore.  A pattern without a slash
# matches the repo ROOT only, not every level: `*.md` does not exclude
# `tests/CHECKLIST.md`, and `certs/` does not exclude
# `crates/admin/src/routes/certs/` (which is *source*, not a certificate
# dump).  Every pattern below that must match at any depth carries an
# explicit `**/` prefix.  `make check-context` pins all of this.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Hidden files and directories ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything whose name starts with a dot: .git, .github, .codegraph,
# .cargo, .env, .gitignore, .cursor, .claude, .aider, .windsurf, .vscode,
# .idea, .zed, .continue, .mcp, .devcontainer, .DS_Store, …
#
# None of it is build input, and all of it is per-machine state.  One rule
# covers the whole class, including tools nobody has installed yet.
#
# If the build ever DOES need a dotfile (e.g. a `.cargo/config.toml`), add
# an explicit `!` re-inclusion for it below — do not weaken this rule.
**/.*

# ── Build outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rebuilt inside the container.
target/
bin/
build/output/
# `assets/app.css` is generated by `make build-ui` on the host; the builder
# stage regenerates it with `tailwindcss --minify` before `cargo build`
# snapshots assets/.
assets/app.css
**/*.rs.bk
**/Cargo.lock.bak

# ── Test and runtime artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated, high churn, never read by the compiler.
coverage/
test-results/
logs/
certs/
certs-staging/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.pem
*.prof

# ── Auxiliary tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The admin UI is built by the standalone tailwindcss/esbuild CLIs, not npm.
node_modules/
dist/
package-lock.json

# ── Documentation and planning ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# `*.md` alone only matches the repo ROOT — nested docs (tests/CHECKLIST.md,
# …) still land in the context.  Use `**/*.md`.
docs/
wip/
tasks/
**/*.md

# ── Host-only operational files ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ansible playbooks — used by `make play` on the host, never by the build.
deploy/
# A second, unreferenced copy of crates/ngx/tests/pebble-root.pem.
test-support/

# ── Deliberately KEPT (see the allow-list above) ───────────────────────────
# The Makefile is one 28 KB file and nothing in the image reads it, but it
# keeps the container's view of the repo identical to a developer's
# checkout.
#
# `ngx.yml` / `tun.yml` are the gateway's runtime config and `rustfmt.toml`
# governs `cargo fmt` — all tiny, all low churn, all "normal code", so they
# stay.  (`.env.example` is a dotfile, so `**/.*` above does drop it; it is
# only ever read by `make env-show` on the host.)
